{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "Mass estimator: off-grid and shifted-mass cells for prior-factor validation",
  "phase": "main_assessment",
  "ademp": {
    "aims": [
      "Test a sech-tilt prior parameter fitted on the operating-range archive at effective SNRs between and beyond the fitting grid.",
      "Test whether the best centre of a two-parameter tilt exp(lam*(sech(log(M/m0))-1)) follows the distribution of true masses, using grids whose masses lie systematically above or below the noise-ratio scale sigma_F/sigma_a."
    ],
    "data_generating_mechanisms": [
      "Newton II is assumed correct. One compatible latent 3D pair per replicate; common direction is used only by the simulator and remains unknown to inference.",
      "Known independent isotropic Gaussian coordinate SD 1 in both channels, one effective reading per channel, R=10000 replicates per cell with fresh seeds. The same replicate-index noise is shared across cells; cells cannot be pooled as independent evidence.",
      "Off-grid: effective SNRs cross [0.5,1.5,2.5,5,10,20] (36 cells); 0.5 lies below the fitting range.",
      "Shifted: heavy cells (F,A)=(A*r,A) and light cells (A,A*r) for A in [0.5,1,1.5,2,3] and r in [2,4,8] (30 cells), so true mass is 2, 4 or 8 times the noise ratio, or its reciprocal."
    ],
    "estimands": [
      "Per cell and K in {1.25,1.5,2}: success probability of each archived rule and of each prior-weighted law; regret against the best archived rule."
    ],
    "methods": [
      "Existing isotropic comparison engine unchanged, saving all trials.",
      "prior_weight_study.py scores declared parameter grids afterwards. For the shifted cells a grid is fitted on replicates [0,5000) and evaluated on [5000,10000); the halves share no replicate."
    ],
    "performance_measures": [
      "Largest cell regret per tolerance and its mean over tolerances; success changes against the unweighted law. Monte Carlo precision per cell success is at most 0.005 at R=10000 and 0.007 for each half."
    ]
  },
  "provenance": {
    "managed_repository": "https://github.com/canvalidk/VD-docs",
    "managed_commit": "8782a293297330f7a354d87ebe62792018fa8866",
    "managed_paths": [
      "Newton-analysis/_dscn_mass_estimator/mass_estimator_law_assumed_correct_steering_2026-09-07.md",
      "Newton-analysis/_dscn_mass_estimator/what_forces_the_ratio_of_means_readout.md",
      "Newton-analysis/_dscn_mass_estimator/mass_estimator_additional_derivations_2026-09-05.md"
    ],
    "methodology": [
      {
        "title": "Morris, White and Crowther: Using simulation studies to evaluate statistical methods",
        "url": "https://doi.org/10.1002/sim.8086"
      },
      {
        "title": "Gneiting: Making and Evaluating Point Forecasts",
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0902"
      }
    ]
  },
  "interpretation": [
    "The shifted grids deliberately break the symmetry of the operating-range grid about the noise-ratio mass; results on them are not averages over any realistic population of experiments.",
    "Every result is conditional on the declared Gaussian isotropic known-noise model."
  ],
